IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hca-dates`
IMPORT `hca-rules`
IMPORT `hca-seat`

-- Health Complaints Act 1995 (Tas) -- worked cases for the complainant's questions (hca-seat.l4), the date helpers
-- (hca-dates.l4) and the rules (hca-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The
-- facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `dates`

#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 24 `months after` (`d` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 24 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 14 `days after` (`d` 20 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 3 1 2026
#ASSERT `the later of` (`d` 1 1 2025) `and` (`d` 2 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 2 1 2025
#ASSERT `the earlier of` (`d` 1 1 2025) `and` (`d` 2 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 1 1 2025

§§ `s 3, Schedule 1 -- health service`

#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `a service at a hospital, health institution or nursing home` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `massage, naturopathy, acupuncture or another natural or alternative health care or diagnostic service` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Included by Schedule 1 Part 1 item 11A though it is not for anyone's health (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `temporary storage of human remains at a hospital or health institution` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `an administrative service directly related to a health service` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `another service for, or purportedly for, the benefit of human health` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Schedule 1 Part 2: the compensation opinions are excluded.
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `an opinion or decision for a claim under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `an opinion or decision for an application under the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational Exposure) Compensation Act 2011` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `a service not for the benefit of human health` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Prescribed by the regulations as not a health service.
#ASSERT `Is this a health service I can complain about` `a service at a hospital, health institution or nursing home` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 22, 22A -- who may complain`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `the health service user` 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) has no age limit: a patient of 10 may complain (finding 1).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `the health service user` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(i): a person appointed by a patient of 14 to 17.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the child appointed to complain for them` 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the child appointed to complain for them` 17 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the child appointed to complain for them` 13 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the child appointed to complain for them` 18 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the child appointed to complain for them` 13 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(ii): a parent of a patient under 14; not of a patient of 14 (finding 1), unless the Commissioner permits.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the child` 13 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the child` 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a parent or guardian of the child` 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d): only an attorney whose authority covers complaints.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `the donee of a power of attorney from the health service user` 80 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `the donee of a power of attorney from the health service user` 80 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person who has the care of the user's affairs under a law or a court order` 80 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (f): both the difficulty and the approval.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the Commissioner approved because the user cannot complain` 80 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a person the Commissioner approved because the user cannot complain` 80 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `a health service provider` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `the Minister, the Health Minister or the Secretary of the Health Department` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (k) closes the list (fork F2); s 22A lets anyone complain of a code-of-conduct breach.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `someone else` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `someone else` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to make this complaint` `someone else` 50 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 23(1), 25(5)(b) -- grounds`

#ASSERT `Is my complaint about a ground the Act covers` `the provider failed to exercise due skill` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint about a ground the Act covers` `the provider unreasonably denied or restricted access to the user's records, or withheld information about the user's condition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint about a ground the Act covers` `the provider acted in another way inconsistent with the Charter` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint about a ground the Act covers` `something else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22A against s 25(5)(b): the text conflicts (finding 2, fork F3).
#ASSERT `Is my complaint about a ground the Act covers` `a health care worker breached a code of conduct, and nothing else` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 23(3)-(5) -- form`

#ASSERT `What form must my complaint take` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `in the form section 23(3) asks for`
#ASSERT `What form must my complaint take` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `accepted orally, and you must put it in writing and sign it if the Commissioner requires`
#ASSERT `What form must my complaint take` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not in that form, and the Commissioner may still accept it`
#ASSERT `What form must my complaint take` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not in that form, and the Commissioner may still accept it`

§§ `s 25(5)(c), (ca), (6) -- time limit`

#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2024) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
-- A health care worker: both clocks, the earlier governs (finding 3).
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 1 6 2023) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2023) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 1 9 2023) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2023) EQUALS `d` 1 6 2025
-- Not a health care worker: only the patient's awareness counts.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 1 9 2023) FALSE (`d` 1 6 2023) EQUALS `d` 1 9 2025

-- Aware 10 March 2024: in time on 10 March 2026, not on 11 March 2026 unless good reason.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2024) (`d` 10 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2024) (`d` 11 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2024) (`d` 11 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2024) (`d` 10 3 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Aware 29 February 2024: in time on 28 February 2026, not on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 28 2 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 29 2 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Complainant aware 1 June 2023, patient 1 September 2023, complaint 15 August 2025: out of time for a health care
-- worker, in time otherwise.
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 9 2023) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2023) (`d` 15 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 9 2023) FALSE (`d` 1 6 2023) (`d` 15 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 25(5)(d)-(j) -- other grounds of dismissal`

#ASSERT `Must my complaint be dismissed on another ground` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my complaint be dismissed on another ground` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A court has commenced to hear the negligence claim (finding 4).
#ASSERT `Must my complaint be dismissed on another ground` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my complaint be dismissed on another ground` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 24, 25(7) -- a requirement for information`

#ASSERT `By when must I meet the requirement after a warning` (`d` 3 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 17 3 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I meet the requirement after a warning` (`d` 20 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 3 1 2026

-- Period ended 1 March 2025; warned 3 March 2025; 14 days end 17 March 2025.
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 18 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 17 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Met on the last of the 14 days; met late but before the day asked about ((d) fails).
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 17 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 19 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Met only after the day asked about: still unsatisfied on that day.
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 25 3 2025) (`d` 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No warning; a warning before the period ended, or on its last day.
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 5 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be dismissed for not meeting the requirement on this day` (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE `any day` (`d` 30 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 25(1), 27 -- assessment`

#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be assessed` (`d` 1 7 2025) 0 0 EQUALS `d` 15 8 2025
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be assessed` (`d` 1 7 2025) 45 0 EQUALS `d` 29 9 2025
-- An extension under (1C) above 45 days counts as 45 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be assessed` (`d` 1 7 2025) 60 0 EQUALS `d` 29 9 2025
#ASSERT `By when must my complaint be assessed` (`d` 1 7 2025) 45 10 EQUALS `d` 9 10 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the assessment` (`d` 20 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 3 1 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I be told of the assessment` (`d` 15 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 29 8 2025

§§ `s 30 -- withdrawal`

#ASSERT `By when must the provider be told I withdrew` TRUE (`d` 10 2 2025) EQUALS JUST (`d` 24 2 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must the provider be told I withdrew` FALSE (`d` 10 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 25(4), 32A, 33, 37, 39 -- conciliation`

#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my complaint go to conciliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Must I attend this conciliation meeting` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I attend this conciliation meeting` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I attend this conciliation meeting` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Notice 1 April 2025 at 9; request 3 April at 9 (48 hours): yes; at 8 (47 hours): no.
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) 9 (`d` 3 4 2025) 9 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) 9 (`d` 3 4 2025) 8 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) 9 (`d` 4 4 2025) 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Across a month end: 31 March at 17 to 2 April at 17.
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` TRUE TRUE (`d` 31 3 2025) 17 (`d` 2 4 2025) 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 4 2025) 9 (`d` 10 4 2025) 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be represented at conciliation` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 4 2025) 9 (`d` 10 4 2025) 9 EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can it be used as evidence in court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can it be used as evidence in court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Verbal agreement 1 May 2025: written on 15 May (the 14th day) binds; on 16 May it does not.
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 15 5 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 16 5 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In writing in time but not put in a binding form (fork F8); reached outside conciliation (s 39(3)).
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 10 5 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is our conciliation agreement binding` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 10 5 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 55(2), 56AAD(2) -- report and statement of decision`

#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the investigation report` `an investigation of my complaint` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the investigation report` `an investigation of an issue or question arising from my complaint` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A code-of-conduct investigation (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the investigation report` `an investigation of a possible breach of a code of conduct by a health care worker` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the investigation report` `an investigation directed by the Health Minister` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will I get a copy of the investigation report` `an investigation of another matter on the Commissioner's own motion` EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Will I get the statement of decision on the order` `a prohibition order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will I get the statement of decision on the order` `a prohibition order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will I get the statement of decision on the order` `an interim prohibition order` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Will I get the statement of decision on the order` `no order` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 56 -- the provider's answer`

-- Received 2 June 2025: 45 days end 17 July 2025; with 15 more, 1 August 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must my provider answer the notice` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 EQUALS `d` 17 7 2025
#ASSERT `By when must my provider answer the notice` (`d` 2 6 2025) TRUE 15 EQUALS `d` 1 8 2025
-- More than 15 days counts as 15; an extension without a request in time does not count (fork F9).
#ASSERT `By when must my provider answer the notice` (`d` 2 6 2025) TRUE 20 EQUALS `d` 1 8 2025
#ASSERT `By when must my provider answer the notice` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 15 EQUALS `d` 17 7 2025

#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 17 7 2025) (`d` 20 7 2025) EQUALS `the provider answered in time`
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 18 7 2025) (`d` 20 7 2025) EQUALS `the provider did not answer in time, an offence with a fine of up to 50 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 FALSE `any day` (`d` 17 7 2025) EQUALS `the provider's time has not yet run out`
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 FALSE `any day` (`d` 18 7 2025) EQUALS `the provider did not answer in time, an offence with a fine of up to 50 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) TRUE 15 TRUE (`d` 1 8 2025) (`d` 5 8 2025) EQUALS `the provider answered in time`
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) TRUE 15 FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 8 2025) EQUALS `the provider's time has not yet run out`
-- Advised on 25 July, asked about 20 July: not yet advised on that day, and the 45 days are over.
#ASSERT `Has my provider answered the notice in time` (`d` 2 6 2025) FALSE 0 TRUE (`d` 25 7 2025) (`d` 20 7 2025) EQUALS `the provider did not answer in time, an offence with a fine of up to 50 penalty units`

